silm:instances_papers_11_base_commutative_diagram_chapters_25_six_step_bridge_deep_dives_sections_01_mereology_six_step_concrete_anchor_5#bodymass_value silm:hasLongDescription "The BodyMass_value is the typed body-mass value 4.2 kg measured at vet visit F11-2026; one specific measurement leg into Mittens_whole. In the paper's apparatus it appears as the symbol 'BodyMass_value', a concrete instance grounded in the Mittens domain story; it serves as the anchor whose semantics every diagram, formula, and prose reference back to." .
